  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Justice has obligated $98.1M in contracts in FY2027 to date. The agency recorded 1,384 awards so far, with an average award size of $70.9K. Obligations fell 99.0% year over year. The DOJ’s fiscal-year obligations for prior years were $9B in FY22, $10B in FY23, $9.3B in FY24, $8.6B in FY25, and $10.2B in FY26. The FY2027 total is a partial, fiscal year to date figure. Top spending categories in FY2027 to date include General Medical and Surgical Hospitals at $12.9M, Other Support Activities for Air Transportation at $12.5M, and Software Publishers at $10.4M, followed by All Other Miscellaneous Food Manufacturing at $10.3M and Offices of Certified Public Accountants at $6.8M. Leading vendors in FY2027 to date include AAR AIRCRAFT SERVICES, INC. at $12.4M, ADVANCED TECHNOLOGIES GROUP LLC at $10.4M, and ERNST & YOUNG LLP at $6.8M. The Department of Justice’s current-year obligations show a much lower dollar total compared with recent full fiscal years.",
