      "q": "How much does Department of Justice spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Justice has obligated $98.1M in contracts in FY2027 to date. The agency recorded 1,384 awards with an average award size of $70.9K. Obligations fell 99.0% year over year, and prior full fiscal-year obligations were $9B in FY22, $10B in FY23, $9.3B in FY24, $8.6B in FY25, and $10.2B in FY26."
